# NYC FLOOD ELIMINATION - THE THREE-LINE HARBOR BARRIER, DESIGNED BY THE PULSE CHIP (DESK LABEL)
**(c) C. MATTHEW BLACKWELL - INDEPENDENT DESIGNER - IDENTITY VERIFICATION BAKED IN**
Designed 2026-11-10 - Filed as EQS-1038 - UNSEALED - NOT BUILT
Name door D-NF1. Design aim in the designer's words: eliminate New York
City flooding. Register-level design under the EQS-1036 discipline,
extending the EQS-1037 NYC-4 gate into a full system. All figures
computed in-run (nyc_flood_run.json); geometry and load inputs are
labelled classes. FLOOD PERFORMANCE IS NOT MEASURED by this design -
see the decider, door D-NF3.

## Design basis (labelled classes)
- Design water: a Sandy-class event (Battery surge ~2.8 m class, total
  water ~4.3 m class) carried to a 5.0 m design class with allowance.
- Gate leaf: 12 m tall class on a sill at -6 m class; crest +6 m class.
- Three lines close the harbor's three entrances; river flow, tide and
  navigation pass through the gate sections in open position.

## The lines (layout classes)
- LINE A - THE NARROWS: 1,600 m class; 8 leaves; 56 fixed caissons.
- LINE B - EAST RIVER NORTH: 600 m class; 4 leaves; 18 caissons.
- LINE C - OUTER HARBOR (SANDY HOOK-ROCKAWAY): 9,000 m class;
  12 leaves; 414 caissons.
System: 566 articles, 1,037,836,800 kg total.

